[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/154790923","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/572#issuecomment-154790923","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/572","id":154790923,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE1NDc5MDkyMw==","user":{"login":"davidzchen","id":5283042,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODMwNDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5283042?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidzchen","html_url":"https://github.com/davidzchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidzchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidzchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidzchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidzchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidzchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidzchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidzchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidzchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidzchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-11-08T09:23:52Z","updated_at":"2015-11-08T09:24:00Z","body":"Thanks for reporting this, @alex!\n\nI don't think the problem is caused by this line:\n\n``` rust\nassert_eq!(\"Hi Rust\", hello.greeting(\"Rust\"));\n```\n\nIn this line, `Greeter::greeting()` is called, which returns a `String`. The only test that is known to fail currently is the `rust_bench_test` in `examples/rust/fibonacci` since `Bencher` in `libtest` is unstable. Perhaps I should disable that test for now.\n\nWhat's curious is that when I run `bazel test //examples/rust/hello_lib:all` on Linux, the tests all pass:\n\n```\n❯❯❯ bazel test //examples/rust/hello_lib:all\n.....\nINFO: Found 2 targets and 3 test targets...\nINFO: Elapsed time: 18.917s, Critical Path: 2.23s\n//examples/rust/hello_lib:greeting_test                                  PASSED in 0.1s\n//examples/rust/hello_lib:hello_lib_doc_test                             PASSED in 0.2s\n//examples/rust/hello_lib:hello_lib_test                                 PASSED in 0.2s\n\nExecuted 3 out of 3 tests: 3 tests pass.\nThere were tests whose specified size is too big. Use the --test_verbose_timeout_warnings command line option to see which ones these are.\n```\n\nHowever, on OS X, there are a number of build errors:\n\n```\n❯❯❯ bazel clean --expunge && bazel test //examples/rust/hello_lib:all\nINFO: Starting clean (this may take a while). Consider using --expunge_async if the clean takes more than several minutes.\n......\nINFO: Found 2 targets and 3 test targets...\nINFO: From Compiling Rust library hello_lib (2 files):\nmkdir: bazel-out/local_darwin-fastbuild/bin/examples/rust/hello_lib/hello_lib.deps: File exists\nERROR: /Volumes/Ocean/Projects/google/bazel/examples/rust/hello_lib/BUILD:11:1: error executing shell command: 'set -e; rm -rf bazel-out/local_darwin-fastbuild/bin/examples/rust/hello_lib/hello_lib.deps; mkdir bazel-out/local_darwin-fastbuild/bin/examples/rust/hello_lib/hello_lib.deps\n LD_LIBRARY_PATH=extern...' failed: bash failed: error executing command /bin/bash -c ... (remaining 1 argument(s) skipped): com.google.devtools.build.lib.shell.BadExitStatusException: Process exited with status 1.\nError reading log file /private/var/tmp/_bazel_dzc/a4c09a1fcefb8b21c5b0e7d7db6f08ba/bazel/bazel-out/local_darwin-fastbuild/testlogs/examples/rust/hello_lib/hello_lib_doc_test/test.log: /private/var/tmp/_bazel_dzc/a4c09a1fcefb8b21c5b0e7d7db6f08ba/bazel/bazel-out/local_darwin-fastbuild/testlogs/examples/rust/hello_lib/hello_lib_doc_test/test.log\nFAIL: //examples/rust/hello_lib:hello_lib_doc_test (see /private/var/tmp/_bazel_dzc/a4c09a1fcefb8b21c5b0e7d7db6f08ba/bazel/bazel-out/local_darwin-fastbuild/testlogs/examples/rust/hello_lib/hello_lib_doc_test/test.log).\nERROR: /Volumes/Ocean/Projects/google/bazel/examples/rust/hello_lib/BUILD:35:1: output 'examples/rust/hello_lib/hello_lib_doc_test/test.log' was not created.\nERROR: /Volumes/Ocean/Projects/google/bazel/examples/rust/hello_lib/BUILD:35:1: not all outputs were created.\nINFO: Elapsed time: 29.038s, Critical Path: 1.39s\n//examples/rust/hello_lib:hello_lib_doc_test                             FAILED in 0.0s\n\nExecuted 1 out of 3 tests: 2 fail to build and 1 fails locally.\n```\n\nThough, when I run `bazel test //examples/rust/...` on Linux, I also see the error where `test.log` is not getting created but only intermittently.\n\nThis seems to be a problem in the rule implementation. I will investigate further.\n\n+@laurentlb for FYI.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/154790923/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"davidzchen","id":5283042,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODMwNDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5283042?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidzchen","html_url":"https://github.com/davidzchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidzchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidzchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidzchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidzchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidzchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidzchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidzchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidzchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidzchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin"